WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:05.588
At the seas with Nemo and friends
at Epcot.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.091
New faces appear every day,

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:13.138
but old friends are never far away
like guest favorite

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.933
Little Joe.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.437
This guy was found alone
in the wild as a baby,

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:24.607
but the team took him in
and gave him the chance to flourish.

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:28.903
I love Joe the Manatee.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.990
He is one of my favorites.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.034
Joe is very charismatic.

00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:36.453
I think he's very handsome.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:38.413
His face is adorable.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:40.415
He's pretty easy going.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:44.502
What is not to love about Joe?

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:50.175
But recently there's been a problem.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:53.178
Despite his name, Lil Joe shouldn't

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:56.181
be so Lil.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.101
Joe's weight is under where
we would like it to be.

00:01:00.101 --> 00:01:02.645
So that's concerning for me.

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:05.565
Yesterday he ate about 30 heads, lettuce
and usually can eat 90.

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:10.236
We want to be able to help him and we can't help him if we don't know what's wrong.

00:01:11.821 --> 00:01:12.405
If only

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.532
manatees could communicate with humans.

00:01:15.825 --> 00:01:16.659
Well.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:21.414
Turns out this clever guy kind of can.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.417
Well, Joe started
taking both of his pectoral flippers

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.753
and putting them in his mouth
and kind of chewing on them.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.924
Sometimes what that behavior tells us
is he maybe uncomfortable in his mouth?

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:35.678
Time for some manatee dentistry.

00:01:36.554 --> 00:01:39.432
And at this dentist, head
protection is a must.

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:44.562
Joe may be underweight,
but that huge tail still packs a punch.

00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:47.148
First, I want to put these under his head.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:55.031
An X-ray reveal anything unusual
with Joe's mouth.

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:58.660
So what is that?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.744
Look at that.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:02.622
Where'd you see this?

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.707
Yeah.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:07.001
Something doesn't look right.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.507
That looks fractured.

00:02:12.507 --> 00:02:14.384
I can see through the tooth.

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.261
It shouldn't
be able to see through the tooth.

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:17.846
It should be pretty solid.

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:21.432
There might be an infection in there
eating away at the base of the tooth,

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:23.184
and that tooth may need to come out.

00:02:23.184 --> 00:02:26.896
If we've been searching for the reason
why he is not eating and that tooth

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.399
Certainly could be it.

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:32.569
You can't really force a 2,000 pound animal
to open his mouth if he doesn’t want to.

00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:35.864
So we're going to ask very nicely

00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:39.742
and hope that he cooperates with us today.

00:02:42.078 --> 00:02:42.579
Okay.

00:02:43.371 --> 00:02:44.164
We're going

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:48.293
to think I wouldn't stick my hands in
just any manatee's mouth.

00:02:48.877 --> 00:02:51.963
I do trust in
Joe much more than any other manatee

00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:00.221
I can easily move

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:04.184
this first molar back and forth with my finger,

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:07.395
which means it needs to come out

00:03:10.565 --> 00:03:12.650
Last time I felt this, it was not mobile.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.653
Like this. So this is different.

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:16.654
Try and

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:22.827
Did you take it out?

00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:23.828
You got it.

00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.371
I think I got it.

00:03:26.122 --> 00:03:27.874
I’d say high 5 but,

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.001
I don't have a hand to spare.

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:31.586
It's awesome.

00:03:31.586 --> 00:03:32.545
Sorry, buddy.

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.171
Let me have it.

00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:33.671
Give it to me.

00:03:33.671 --> 00:03:36.090
I get the forceps.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.092
Oh, my God. They're gone.

00:03:38.092 --> 00:03:38.927
Oh, my God. I got it.

00:03:38.927 --> 00:03:39.594
You got it.

00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:41.971
I got it. It's on my fingers.
I'm just trying not to drop it.

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:44.265
Don't let it go.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:45.808
Don't drop it when you take it out.

00:03:47.018 --> 00:03:50.605
Oh. Oh, wow.

00:03:50.772 --> 00:03:53.858
Gosh, we just pulled that tooth out

00:03:54.984 --> 00:03:57.111
Do you want to pull my tooth out? Wow.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.114
So I think it was just that one tooth

00:04:00.114 --> 00:04:01.699
That was giving him trouble.

00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:03.785
They're made to lose their teeth
frequently.

00:04:04.118 --> 00:04:05.411
Usually they lose them on their own.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.538
And you don't need to go in
and pull them out.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.250
If this manatee starts eating.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.919
We are throwing a party.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.128
Good job, Joe.

00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:18.841
the next step is to get back in the water
and see if he wants to eat.

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.094
Should be very exciting.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:24.722
So you can do it, big guy.

